Reading: in every row the inequality holds from some m0 on (for c' < c it holds once
2^((c-c')m) exceeds k times a constant), as the proofs need; m0 grows as
c' approaches c and as c shrinks.  The separations are asymptotic: below m0 a clocked hypothesis
may label every short sentence correctly.
